WEBVTT

00:00:58.518 --> 00:01:00.488
Why can't we build tiny robots?

00:01:01.205 --> 00:01:03.587
Well, I'm not the only one
to have this idea.

00:01:03.611 --> 00:01:06.270
In fact, in the last, oh, few years,

00:01:06.294 --> 00:01:09.247
researchers around the world
have taken up the task

00:01:09.271 --> 00:01:11.346
of trying to build robots

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:14.200
that are so small that they can't be seen.

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.878
And what we're going
to tell you about today

00:01:16.902 --> 00:01:18.750
is an effort at Cornell University

00:01:18.774 --> 00:01:21.082
and now at the University of Pennsylvania

00:01:21.106 --> 00:01:23.461
to try to build tiny robots.

00:01:24.064 --> 00:01:25.896
OK, so that's the goal.

00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:27.875
But how do we do it?

00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:30.699
How do we go about building tiny robots?